 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance authorizing The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County to accept new sanitary sewer main, sanitary sewer manholes, vertical relocation of sanitary sewer manhole and easements, for property located at 2826 Hartford Drive (MWS Project No. 25-SL-231 and Proposal No. 2026M062ES-001).\n..body\nWHEREAS, the acceptance of approximately 156 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), two new sanitary sewer manholes, vertical relocation of an existing manhole and easements, for property located at 2826 Hartford Drive, is needed to construct Project No. 25SL231; and,\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Planning Commission approved mandatory referral No. 2026M062ES-001 on July 23, 2026, for the acceptance of said sanitary sewer main, sanitary sewer manholes, vertical relocation of existing manhole and easements. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThe Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County is authorized to accept approximately 156 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), two new sanitary sewer manholes, the vertical relocation of an existing manhole and easements, for property located at 2826 Hartford Drive, as shown on Exhibit 1, which is attached hereto and incorporated by reference.\nMap & Parcel: \t\t\t\tAddress:\n11910017500\t\t\t\t\t2826 Hartford Drive\nSection 2.\tThe Directors of Water and Sewerage Services and Public Property Administration are authorized to execute such documents as may be necessary and appropriate to carry out the acceptance authorized by this ordinance. \nSection 3.\tAmendments to this legislation shall be approved by resolution.\nSection 4.\tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of The Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it. \n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance accepts approximately 156 linear feet of new eight-inch sanitary sewer main (PVC), two new sanitary sewer manholes, the vertical relocation of an existing manhole and easements, for property located at 2826 Hartford Drive.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\nFiscal Note: This ordinance has no cost to Metro. Donated easements have no market value according to the Department of Water and Sewerage Services.\n\n"
}
